  "summary": "neroteam-v1 executes an encrypted, anti-analysis-guarded payload on import",
  "details": "nero/__init__.py imports nero.main, which at import time runs an anti-analysis guard (_guard) that measures timing, checks sys.gettrace(), scans PATH/sys.executable/processor for sandbox/virtualbox/vmware/qemu/wine/hyperv/xen and exits if any match, then clears settrace and the current frame's f_trace. It then base64-decodes a ~227KB in-package blob, decrypts it with a hardcoded custom RC4-style stream cipher keyed by 'ChaChaSecret256BitsKey!', and passes the plaintext to exec(). The decrypted bytes are not present on PyPI as readable source, so every install that imports the package runs opaque author-controlled code with no user consent or review. The package advertises itself as a 'Free Fire account generator' with '2000 Threads / 100.000 IP Pool / Rare Account Detection' in README and pyproject.",
